title smelt — target architecture (structure)\n\
Decisions and rationale live in **ARCHITECTURE.md**; sequencing in **REFACTOR.md**.

legend right
  **Target organization (post P12.A):**
  - `core` — frontend-agnostic; no terminal imports, no `crossterm`,
    no editor / renderer deps.
  - `smelt-buffer` — shared data layer: `Buffer`, extmarks, undo,
    `Theme`, `Style`, `Color`, clipboard, attachments. Both the
    renderer and editor depend on it; pure data, no terminal calls.
  - `smelt-term` — pure terminal renderer: `Grid`, `Compositor`,
    `LayoutTree<PaintId>`, `flush_diff`, chrome paint, `paint_layout_tree`.
    No `Window`, no vim, no editor concepts. Standalone; usable as a
    TUI library (e.g. by `tcloc`).
  - `smelt-edit` — editor layer over `smelt-term`: `Window`,
    `DrawContext`, `Buffer` dispatch, vim modes, callbacks, overlays,
    focus + capture + click-tracking. The `Ui` struct ties windows to
    layout and routes events; its renderer is a `smelt_term::Compositor`.
  - `tui` — terminal frontend; depends on `core`, `smelt-edit`,
    `smelt-buffer`, `smelt-term`, and `crossterm`. Owns `PaintRegistry`
    (Lua-side `smelt.paint` dispatch) and `TuiApp::resolve_leaf_id`
    which maps raw `u64` paint ids to `LeafKind::Window` / `LeafKind::Paint`.
  - `engine` / `protocol` — unchanged; LLM core + wire types.

  A GUI or web frontend uses `core` directly and ignores
  `smelt-{term,edit}`. A non-editor TUI consumer (treemap, dashboard)
  uses `smelt-term` directly with its own paint dispatcher.

  **`Buffer` lives in `smelt-buffer`** (was: `core`). It is pure
  data — lines, extmarks, namespaces, undo. Zero terminal deps.
  Headless reads transcript content through the same surface as the
  TUI does. Parser *implementations* (markdown / diff / syntax /
  bash) stay in `tui` because they pull from
  `tui::content::highlight::*` (syntect, inline markdown, diff LCS).

  **Lua's drawing context is full, not partial.** Tool / dialog /
  statusline `render` callbacks receive a `Buffer` userdata with the
  full Buffer API (set_lines / add_highlight / set_extmark / attach /
  namespaces / virt-text). No `RenderCtx`-style enum-of-allowed-methods.
  Shipped Rust renderers (smelt.bash.render, smelt.diff.render,
  smelt.syntax.render, smelt.notebook.render) sit on top of the Buffer
  API as conveniences, not in front of it.

  **No tool/command/dialog/mode name matching in Rust.** A `match name {
  "bash" => … }` over a Lua-registered identifier is a bug. The
  registration table carries the metadata; Rust calls through it.

  **Plugin-author surface (P9.f–y, landed).** Namespaces are integer
  handles minted by `smelt.buf.create_namespace`. Extmark API is one
  keyset call mirroring nvim verbatim (`hl_eol`, `hl_mode`,
  `virt_text_pos`, gravity, priority, etc.). Plugins live in
  `~/.config/smelt/` AND project-local `<cwd>/.smelt/` (trust-gated
  via SHA-256). Tool files auto-register on require. Cell
  subscribers see (new, old); user-namespaced cells via
  `smelt.cell.user(...)`. `require` searches workspace + user
  runtime before embedded fallback (P9.j). Read-only tools opt into
  parallel execution (P9.k). Permission defaults declared in Lua via
  `permission_defaults` / `default_allow` (P9.y). Provider middleware
  remains **deferred** (P9.i — speculative seam, lands when first
  consumer materializes).
end legend

' =====================================================================
' LUA — entire UX
' =====================================================================
package "runtime/lua/smelt/  (UX layer — the whole user-facing surface)" as LUA #FFEFE0 {

  class "widgets/*.lua" as LWID <<Lua>> {
    input, options, list, picker,
    cmdline, statusline, notification
    — keymap recipes for Windows
  }
  class "dialog.lua" as LDLGHELP <<Lua>> {
    splits-edit OR Overlay helper
    one question per dialog
    (no tab strip in framework)
  }
  class "dialogs/*.lua" as LDLG <<Lua>> {
    confirm, permissions, agents,
    rewind, resume
    multi-question flow = Lua
    loop opening N dialogs
  }
  class "status.lua"  as LSTAT <<Lua>> {
    statusline spec (segments)
    segments bind to Cells:
      { bind = "now", fmt = … }
      { bind = "agent_mode" }
      …
    escape hatch:
      { call = fn, deps = {…} }
      ' fn re-runs only when one of
      ' deps' cells changes
  }
  class "modes.lua"   as LMOD  <<Lua>>
  class "transcript.lua" as LTX <<Lua>> {
    buf.attach { parser="markdown",
                 on_block=… }
  }
  class "diff.lua" as LDIFF <<Lua>> {
    buf.attach { parser="diff",
                 on_block=… }
  }
  class "commands.lua" as LCMD <<Lua>>
  class "commands/messages.lua" as LMSG <<Lua>> {
    /messages — read-only
    bottom-docked viewer over
    `core::Messages`. Composes
    smelt.buf.create({readonly=true})
    + dialog.open with
    border = "top", title.
  }
  class "tools/*.lua" as LTOOLS <<Lua>> {
    bash, read_file, write_file,
    edit_file, glob, grep, web_fetch,
    web_search, notebook, agent, …
  }
  class "plugins/*.lua" as LPLG <<Lua>>
  class "colorschemes/*.lua" as LCS <<Lua>>
  class "paint.lua" as LPAINT <<Lua>> {
    smelt.paint.register(fn) -> paint_id
    smelt.paint.unregister(id)
    ' Allocates PaintId via Rust registry;
    ' callback receives GridSlice userdata.
  }
  class "examples/snake.lua" as LSNAKE <<Lua>> {
    dogfood widget; two paint regions
    (playfield + perf panel);
    timer-driven animation at ~60fps.
    Not autoloaded.
  }
}

